  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 21-layer Ta2O5/SiO2 Fabry-Perot bandpass filter on fused silica substrate for 1550 nm LiDAR receiver. Incident medium is air. Initialize from the R3 best candidate thicknesses: [173.25, 324.48, 150.60, 227.07, 188.79, 260.87, 173.64, 111.52, 113.01, 182.11, 253.25, 251.08, 301.44, 148.31, 404.39, 392.31, 167.99, 366.33, 206.82, 195.34, 248.81] nm. Freeze layers 1-7 and 13-21 at these values. Optimize only layers 8-12 with bounds ±2 nm around [111.52, 113.01, 182.11, 253.25, 251.08] nm respectively. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with minimum step resolution 0.25 nm. Evaluate coherent TMM transmittance spectrum from 1300-1800 nm at normal incidence, unpolarized. Score based on high transmission at 1550 nm and suppression in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
